{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "UkKVDhfcB3", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Tom Brokaw (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 40, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763130, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "VwSNqxl3va", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "Decision 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / Kerry\u2019s War Record", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced. \n (White House: David Gregory) The continuing flap over the political ads bashing Senator John Kerry\u2019s war record featured; details given of President Bush\u2019s denouncement of attack ads by outside interest groups known as 527s; anti-Bush ad shown. [In Crawford, Texas, BUSH \u2013 says unregulated soft money is wrong for the process; says Kerry served admirably.] [Former Senator Bob DOLE \u2013 states not every one of these people can be Republican liars.] [Senator John EDWARDS \u2013 says Bush faced his moment of truth & he failed.] [Political analyst Stuart ROTHENBERG&#134;- outlines how the Bush campaign is trying to redefine Kerry.]", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63040.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763131, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "6cVAhTEAxW", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "Economy / Overtime Rules", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced. \n (Atlanta: Tom Costello) The controversial change in the rules for overtime pay examined; scenes shown of labor rallies in Miami & Washington; details given about the restrictions of the new \u201cfair pay\u201d rules. [Senator John EDWARDS \u2013 criticizes the change.] [Assistant Secretary of Labor Victoria LIPNIC&#134;- says the new rules will provide more overtime protection.] [ANALYST \u2013 notes uncertainty about how the rules will work.] \n (Studio: Tom Brokaw) Further information on msnbc.com noted.", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63180.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763132, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "NUmjCBSU7N", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "Iraq / Prisoner Abuse Scandal", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report that shrapnel from US bombing near the Imam Ali mosque in Najaf, Iraq, hit the shrine\u2019s dome, and the announcement from S/Sgt. Ivan \u201cChip\u201d Frederick that he will plead guilty to charges of prisoner abuse at Abu Ghraib prison reported; scenes shown. \n (Mannheim, Germany: Fred Francis) The Pentagon\u2019s report on the prisoner abuse scandal, authored by former Secretary of Defense James Schlesinger&#134;&#134;, previewed; details given of the report\u2019s charges of leadership failures by Brig. Gen. Janis Karpinski, Col. Thomas Pappas, Lt. Gen. Ricardo Sanchez & others. [Defense attorney Guy WOMACK&#134;- says it would be laughable to conclude that the MPs acted with no direction from above.]", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63310.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763133, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "RXdNJixGbV", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "September 11 / Commission Report", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced.   (Washington: Pete Williams) The 9/11 Commission\u2019s finding that some of the September 11 hijackers had terrorism warnings on their visas that were not caught by the intelligence community or explained to border agents featured; statement from captured terrorist Khalid Shaikh Mohammed on increased difficulty for Al Qaeda due to closer attention to immigrants noted. [9/11 Commission Christopher KOJM&#134;- criticizes the intelligence community for not making information available.] [Department of Homeland Security Adm. James LOY&#134;- says people, cargo & conveyances are being examined & screened more effectively.]", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63460.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763134, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "fEGAmoC8jq", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Tom Brokaw)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63600.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763135, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "fXHAj5v1gJ", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Frontline; Metamucil; Imitrex; American Egg Board; Detrol; \"Today.\")", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63610.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763136, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-23", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 763130, "segment_id": "CULx3D1Hhl", "segment_broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "segment_title": "In Depth (Olympic Games)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced. \n (Athens: Brian Williams) Controversial episodes from the Olympic Games in Athens, Greece reviewed; details given of the controversy in gymnastics that erupted when the crowd disagreed with the judges\u2019 scoring, of the status of the debate over the gold medal won by US gymnast Paul Hamm and the admission of a US trainer that he gave a sample of a designer steroid to the US Anti-Doping Agency; photos & scenes shown. [\u201cLos Angeles Times\u201d Alan ABRAHAMSON&#134;- notes the negative impact of the doping scandal on the sport of track & field.] \n (Saratoga, California: Anne Thompson) The challenge for US Olympic wrestler Patricia Miranda to overcome her father\u2019s opposition to her participation in the sport featured; scenes & photos shown of Miranda wrestling. [MIRANDA \u2013 comments.] [Father Jose MIRANDA \u2013 jokes about being a \u201cmale chauvinist pig\u201d; comments on watching his daughter wrestle for the US.] [Former college coach Chris HORPEL&#134;- comments on Miranda.] \n (Athens: Brian Williams) Miranda\u2019s bronze medal in her match noted.", "segment_duration": 320, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63750.0", "legacy_segment_id": 763137, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "X3P0uOm27A", "broa